			<div class="content" id="post-content-2523672">
									

<p>I really, really want to like this. The little reminders to the reader coupled with the subject material do a nice job conveying something that is outwardly prosaic and kind of strange, with undercurrents that something is very, very wrong. Great mood throughout.</p>
<p>Then the mystery and everything else gets sapped when we get a sort of half-hearted GoI explanation tacked on it. I can't downvote something that I enjoyed as much as I did about 80% throughout, but I can't upvote with that sour note at the end, either.</p>

